nodes.body:
@EazyReal . Thanks for carrying the validation-boundary approach from #27257 into this PR. The current direction matches the call-path analysis I raised there.

One thing that may still be worth adding is a behavior-level regression test that exercises the actual `n > 1` fan-out path in the tokenizer manager, rather than only indexing the original `batch_size` entries directly. That would verify that each copied sibling retains the correct per-sample session metadata and that the expansion never relies on modulo indexing.

I’d be happy to contribute that test if you think it fits the scope of this PR. I don’t have permission to add the `run-ci` label, so a maintainer would still need to do that.

